 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 1.76,
   "text": "The planet with no sun."
  },
  {
   "start": 2.82,
   "end": 4.54,
   "text": "Imagine a planet with no sun."
  },
  {
   "start": 5.06,
   "end": 9.06,
   "text": "No sunrise, no sunset, no daytime, ever."
  },
  {
   "start": 9.68,
   "end": 13.8,
   "text": "Just endless darkness drifting through space all alone."
  },
  {
   "start": 14.26,
   "end": 16.58,
   "text": "And scientists think there could be billions of them."
  },
  {
   "start": 17.02,
   "end": 18.2,
   "text": "Luna, grab your flashlight."
  },
  {
   "start": 18.68,
   "end": 20.14,
   "text": "This one's going to be dark."
  },
  {
   "start": 20.82,
   "end": 22.74,
   "text": "Most planets travel around a star,"
  },
  {
   "start": 23.04,
   "end": 25.0,
   "text": "but some don't have a star at all."
  },
  {
   "start": 25.76,
   "end": 27.26,
   "text": "Scientists call them rogue planets."
  },
  {
   "start": 27.72,
   "end": 29.08,
   "text": "They wander through the galaxy"
  },
  {
   "start": 29.08,
   "end": 31.36,
   "text": "like a lost ball rolling forever."
  },
  {
   "start": 31.94,
   "end": 34.22,
   "text": "So how does a planet lose its sun?"
  },
  {
   "start": 34.9,
   "end": 37.54,
   "text": "Many may have been born around a star, just like Earth."
  },
  {
   "start": 38.16,
   "end": 40.38,
   "text": "Then a giant planet came too close."
  },
  {
   "start": 40.82,
   "end": 43.7,
   "text": "Its gravity pushed the smaller planet right out of its home."
  },
  {
   "start": 43.96,
   "end": 46.38,
   "text": "Like getting kicked out of the group chat forever."
  },
  {
   "start": 47.6,
   "end": 49.06,
   "text": "Okay, Luna, let's find one."
  },
  {
   "start": 49.5,
   "end": 52.14,
   "text": "But how do you find a planet that doesn't shine?"
  },
  {
   "start": 52.84,
   "end": 56.48,
   "text": "Sometimes a rogue planet passes in front of a faraway star."
  },
  {
   "start": 56.48,
   "end": 59.64,
   "text": "Its gravity bends the light like a magnifying glass."
  },
  {
   "start": 60.04,
   "end": 62.04,
   "text": "For a moment, the star looks brighter."
  },
  {
   "start": 62.5,
   "end": 65.72,
   "text": "That tiny flash tells scientists something is there."
  },
  {
   "start": 66.22,
   "end": 67.5,
   "text": "Found one, let's land."
  },
  {
   "start": 68.4,
   "end": 70.14,
   "text": "Careful, Luna, it's freezing."
  },
  {
   "start": 70.76,
   "end": 73.6,
   "text": "With no sun, it could be much colder than Antarctica."
  },
  {
   "start": 74.28,
   "end": 76.4,
   "text": "Luna, why did you bring sunscreen?"
  },
  {
   "start": 76.98,
   "end": 77.88,
   "text": "There's no sun."
  },
  {
   "start": 78.42,
   "end": 79.46,
   "text": "But here's the surprise."
  },
  {
   "start": 79.94,
   "end": 81.82,
   "text": "Some scientists think a rogue planet"
  },
  {
   "start": 81.82,
   "end": 83.74,
   "text": "could still be warm deep inside."
  },
  {
   "start": 83.74,
   "end": 86.58,
   "text": "Heat from its core, trapped under thick ice,"
  },
  {
   "start": 86.84,
   "end": 89.2,
   "text": "might keep a hidden ocean of liquid water."
  },
  {
   "start": 89.74,
   "end": 91.3,
   "text": "Luna, shine your light down here."
  },
  {
   "start": 91.68,
   "end": 92.4,
   "text": "Do you hear that?"
  },
  {
   "start": 93.02,
   "end": 94.58,
   "text": "Crack, the ice is breaking."
  },
  {
   "start": 95.0,
   "end": 96.44,
   "text": "Run, Luna, back to the ship."
  },
  {
   "start": 97.58,
   "end": 99.32,
   "text": "Phew, that was close."
  },
  {
   "start": 100.02,
   "end": 101.34,
   "text": "Okay, let's be honest."
  },
  {
   "start": 101.82,
   "end": 103.5,
   "text": "Nobody has visited a rogue planet."
  },
  {
   "start": 104.0,
   "end": 106.0,
   "text": "Nobody knows if any have hidden oceans."
  },
  {
   "start": 106.54,
   "end": 109.36,
   "text": "These are ideas from telescope data and computer models."
  },
  {
   "start": 109.74,
   "end": 112.58,
   "text": "And new telescopes are getting ready to find many more."
  },
  {
   "start": 112.58,
   "end": 113.74,
   "text": "Think about it."
  },
  {
   "start": 114.16,
   "end": 116.84,
   "text": "Somewhere out there, a planet drifts through the dark,"
  },
  {
   "start": 117.22,
   "end": 118.24,
   "text": "never seeing a sunrise."
  },
  {
   "start": 118.92,
   "end": 122.14,
   "text": "And here we are, with a brand new sunrise every day."
  },
  {
   "start": 122.7,
   "end": 124.74,
   "text": "And here's the thing, billions of planets,"
  },
  {
   "start": 125.08,
   "end": 126.56,
   "text": "and not one of them can care."
  },
  {
   "start": 127.02,
   "end": 127.8,
   "text": "But you can."
  },
  {
   "start": 128.24,
   "end": 130.64,
   "text": "Don't ever forget how special that makes you."
  },
  {
   "start": 131.28,
   "end": 132.98,
   "text": "Space is truly amazing."
  },
  {
   "start": 133.42,
   "end": 135.08,
   "text": "And this is only the beginning."
  }
 ]
}